    {
      "name": "ke_ecs_commands",
      "doc": "A queue of structural mutations. Every operation records its intent and returns; none changes the world while it runs. The queue is applied, in the order the operations were recorded, by whoever owns it, and an operation\u0027s effect is not observable before then. A caller needing a change visible at once uses ke_ecs, which mutates immediately. Recording never touches the world, so these operations may be called while other code reads it. The queue is applied while nothing else runs. An implementation that cannot accept an operation returns its code, logs the reason, and leaves the queue unchanged: KE_RESULT_NOT_SUPPORTED in a phase that may not change structure, KE_RESULT_OUT_OF_MEMORY when the queue cannot grow.",
